A semiconductor device includes:

- a substrate having first and second substrate regions spaced apart from each other;
- a plurality of wire patterns extending between the first and second substrate regions and suspended above the substrate;
- gate insulating films surrounding respective portions of the wire patterns;
- first and second gate electrodes extending across and intersecting the wire patterns over the gate insulating films; and
- gate spacers disposed on sidewalls of the first and second gate electrodes.

The first gate electrode includes a metal oxide film, which may function as part of its work-function-control or conductive gate structure.
